$$
\left(\frac{20}{3} - \lambda\right)\left(-\frac{14}{3} - \lambda\right) - \left(\frac{8}{3}\right)\left(-\frac{26}{3}\right) = 0
$$

Solving this equation yields the eigenvalues:
$$
\lambda = \frac{2}{3} \left(3 \pm i \sqrt{41}\right)
$$

Thus, the eigenvalues are:
$$
\left\{\frac{2}{3} \left(3 - i \sqrt{41}\right), \frac{2}{3} \left(3 + i \sqrt{41}\right)\right\}
$$

